🐛 Describe the bug
libtorch_cpu doesn't export c10::VaryingShape<c10::Stride>::merge:
$ nm -gDC  libtorch_cpu.so|grep VaryingShape|grep merge
0000000001b36d90 W c10::VaryingShape<bool>::merge(c10::VaryingShape<bool> const&) const
0000000001b36730 W c10::VaryingShape<long>::merge(c10::VaryingShape<long> const&) const
0000000001b37080 W c10::VaryingShape<unsigned long>::merge(c10::VaryingShape<unsigned long> const&) const
0000000001b36a50 W c10::VaryingShape<c10::ShapeSymbol>::merge(c10::VaryingShape<c10::ShapeSymbol> const&) const

which can cause a linking error:
#include <torch/torch.h>

int main(int ac, char **av) {

  c10::VaryingShape<c10::Stride> shape1(c10::Stride(3, true, 1));
  c10::VaryingShape<c10::Stride> shape2(c10::Stride(2, true, 1));
  c10::VaryingShape<c10::Stride> shape3 = shape1.merge(shape2);
  std::cout << shape3;
}
a.cpp:(.text+0x1aa): undefined reference to `c10::VaryingShape<c10::Stride>::merge(c10::VaryingShape<c10::Stride> const&) const'

Versions
libtorch version: 2.2.2
